  "bodyHtml": "<main class=\"main\"><section  class=\"cb-hero cb-hero--type-three cb-hero--align-centre  cb-hero6a0df92780863\" data-delay=\"2500\" data-loop=\"1\" data-autoplay=\"1\"><div class=\"cb-hero__container\"><div class=\"cb-hero__text-block\"><div><h3 class=\"cb-hero__pre-heading\">\nMY TOP 10</h3><h1 class=\"cb-hero__heading\">\nVisual Studio Code Extensions</h1></div></div></div></section><section class=\"c-post-info\"><div class=\"c-post-info__container\"><p>\n<span class=\"c-post-info__read-time\"></span> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Updated&nbsp;<span class=\"c-post-info__date\">01.06.22</span></p></div></section><section  class=\"cb-text-box cb-text-box6a0df927809b5 cb-text-box--type-one cb-text-box--align-left\" style=\"\"><div class=\"cb-text-box__container padding-top-md padding-bottom-md\"><div class=\"cb-text-box__text\"><p>The other day someone in our work chat asked about what extensions they should install on a fresh copy of Visual Studio Code, so I gave them a list of my favourite ones that I use all the time. I later realised that I gave them exactly 10 different ones, so I thought it would make a great top 10 to help others.</p><p>I&#8217;ve tried to put them in an order of importance or value, but this is obviously very subjective and they&#8217;re all amazing.</p><p>So here are my top 10 favourite VS Code extensions!</p><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions.png\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-2184 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions.png\" alt=\"Top ten visual studio code extensions\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" data-srcset=\"/media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions.png 1080w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-300x300.png 300w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-1024x1024.png 1024w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-150x150.png 150w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-768x768.png 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px\" / srcset=\"/media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions.png 1080w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-300x300.png 300w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-1024x1024.png 1024w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-150x150.png 150w, /media/2022/06/top-vscode-entensions-768x768.png 768w\"></p><h2>1. Live Server</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/vscode-live-server-animated-demo.gif\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"width-100 aligncenter wp-image-2166 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/vscode-live-server-animated-demo.gif\" alt=\"Live server vscode extension demo\" width=\"896\" height=\"480\" /></p><p><a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ritwickdey.LiveServer\">Live Server</a> is probably one of my most used extensions, mainly for its ease of use. You just click one button and you get your code to open up in your browser of choice, and it auto reloads when it detects changes.</p><p>Perfect for static projects like HTML Emails.</p><h2>2. Code Spell Checker</h2><p>These days we have spell checkers built into pretty much everything, but not our code editors for some reason. That is why this is an extension that I recommend to people the most. Check out <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=streetsidesoftware.code-spell-checker\">Code Spell Checker</a> whether you&#8217;re a fantastic speller or not, it allows you to quickly spot spelling mistakes in any code you open at a glance which is so handy.</p><h2>3. Highlight Matching Tag</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/highlight-matching-tag-demo.gif\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"width-100 aligncenter wp-image-2168 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/highlight-matching-tag-demo.gif\" alt=\"Demo of highlight matching tag extension\" width=\"529\" height=\"306\" /></p><p>VSCode comes with some highlight matching built-in, but it&#8217;s fairly basic. So <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=vincaslt.highlight-matching-tag\">Highlight Matching Tag</a> takes this a step further.</p><h2>4. Auto Rename Tag</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/usage.gif\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"width-100 aligncenter wp-image-2169 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/usage.gif\" alt=\"auto rename tag demo\" width=\"884\" height=\"454\" /></p><p>This plugin just makes your life so much easier. Even though having your code automatically rename your tags may seem to be such a small quality of life improvement, it really goes a long way. Check out <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=formulahendry.auto-rename-tag\">Auto Rename Tag</a> for yourself, you&#8217;ll enjoy it.</p><h2>5. GitLens</h2><p>If you work in a team, <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=eamodio.gitlens\">GitLens</a> is so valuable in how it helps you by showing who changed what and when the code was updated. It has way more features that I&#8217;ve never even used before, but after having a good look at its page on the marketplace, I will be diving into them.</p><p>In addition, it&#8217;s also wonderfully customisable so you can tailor it to exactly how you desire. That goes for most of these plugins on this list too.</p><h2>6. Indent-rainbow</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54.png\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"width-100 aligncenter wp-image-2171 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54.png\" alt=\"Screenshot showing how indent rainbow looks\" width=\"842\" height=\"608\" data-srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54.png 842w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54-300x217.png 300w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54-768x555.png 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 842px) 100vw, 842px\" / srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54.png 842w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54-300x217.png 300w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.14.54-768x555.png 768w\"></p><p><a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=oderwat.indent-rainbow\">Indent-rainbow</a> is a great little extension that just subtly adds some extra colours to VS Code in order to make indentation more readable. It really helps you narrow down where you are in your code block faster.</p><h2>7. Prettier</h2><p><a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=esbenp.prettier-vscode\">Prettier</a> is one of the most popular plugins on VS Code, and it&#8217;s no surprise because who doesn&#8217;t want nicely formatted code? It can be really useful for teams who use it on a project as it will help enforce a consistent coding style.</p><h2>8. Better comments</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04.png\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"width-100 aligncenter wp-image-2172 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04.png\" alt=\"Demo of better comments\" width=\"862\" height=\"632\" data-srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04.png 862w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04-300x220.png 300w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04-768x563.png 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 862px) 100vw, 862px\" / srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04.png 862w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04-300x220.png 300w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.19.04-768x563.png 768w\"></p><p>Having well-commented code is very important for your team&#8217;s sake, as well as your own. We&#8217;ve probably all been there &#8211; we create something complicated in JS and then have to go back to it a year later and not know what the hell is going on. Well, you need comments, and not just that, <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=aaron-bond.better-comments\">Better Comments</a>.</p><h2>9. Dracula Theme</h2><p>This one is completely personal preference, but <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=dracula-theme.theme-dracula\">Dracula</a> is my favourite theme for coding. I just love it, along with nearly 8 million other developers who&#8217;ve installed the dark theme.</p><h2>10. Material Icon Theme</h2><p><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53.png\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"max-width-400 aligncenter wp-image-2173 size-full\" data-src=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53.png\" alt=\"Demo of better comments plugin\" width=\"438\" height=\"536\" data-srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53.png 438w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53-245x300.png 245w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 438px) 100vw, 438px\" / srcset=\"/media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53.png 438w, /media/2022/05/Screenshot-2022-05-28-at-13.20.53-245x300.png 245w\"></p><p>Going a step further, we have <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PKief.material-icon-theme\">Material Icon Theme</a> which adds nice looking icons to files and folders for VS Code, to really makes them stand out.</p><h2>Bonus</h2><p>As a bonus, don&#8217;t forget to install <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Shan.code-settings-sync\">Settings Sync</a> so you can automatically bring your setup to a new machine with ease.</p><p>What are some of your favourite extensions to use?</p></div></div></section><section class=\"cb-next-post cb-next-post--type-one\"><div class=\"cb-next-post__container padding-top-md padding-bottom-md\"><div class=\"cb-next-post__prev\"><p>Previous post:</p><p class=\"cb-next-post__title\"><a href=\"/blog/tutorial-how-to-create-a-wordpress-plugin/\" rel=\"prev\">Tutorial &#8211; How to create a WordPress Plugin</a></p></div><div class=\"cb-next-post__next\"><p>Next post:</p><p class=\"cb-next-post__title\"><a href=\"/blog/oh-my-ai-cool-uses-of-artificial-intelligence/\" rel=\"next\">OH MY AI &#8211; Cool uses of Artificial Intelligence</a></p></div></section><section class=\"cb-comments cb-comments--type-one\"><div class=\"cb-comments__container padding-top-md padding-bottom-md\"><div id=\"respond\" class=\"comment-respond\"><h3 id=\"reply-title\" class=\"comment-reply-title\">Leave a Reply <small><a rel=\"nofollow\" id=\"cancel-comment-reply-link\" href=\"/blog/my-top-10-best-vs-code-extensions/#respond\" style=\"display:none;\">Cancel reply</a></small></h3><form action=\"https://daltonwalsh.com/wp-comments-post.php\" method=\"post\" id=\"commentform\" class=\"comment-form\"><p class=\"comment-notes\"><span id=\"email-notes\">Your email address will not be published.</span> <span class=\"required-field-message\">Required fields are marked <span class=\"required\">*</span></span></p><p class=\"comment-form-comment\"><label for=\"comment\">Comment <span class=\"required\">*</span></label><textarea id=\"comment\" name=\"comment\" cols=\"45\" rows=\"8\" maxlength=\"65525\" required=\"required\"></textarea></p><p class=\"comment-form-author\"><label for=\"author\">Name <span class=\"required\">*</span></label> <input id=\"author\" name=\"author\" type=\"text\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"245\" autocomplete=\"name\" required=\"required\" /></p><p class=\"comment-form-email\"><label for=\"email\">Email <span class=\"required\">*</span></label> <input id=\"email\" name=\"email\" type=\"text\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"100\" aria-describedby=\"email-notes\" autocomplete=\"email\" required=\"required\" /></p><p class=\"comment-form-url\"><label for=\"url\">Website</label> <input id=\"url\" name=\"url\" type=\"text\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"url\" /></p><p class=\"comment-form-cookies-consent\"><input id=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\" name=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\" type=\"checkbox\" value=\"yes\" /> <label for=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\">Save my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment.</label></p><p class=\"form-submit\"><input